A [Narcissistic Number](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narcissistic_number) is a positive number which is the sum of its own digits, each raised to the power of the number of digits in a given base. In this Kata, we will restrict ourselves to decimal (base 10).

For example, take 153 (3 digits):
```
    1^3 + 5^3 + 3^3 = 1 + 125 + 27 = 153
```
and 1634 (4 digits):
```
    1^4 + 6^4 + 3^4 + 4^4 = 1 + 1296 + 81 + 256 = 1634
```

The Challenge:

Your code must return **true or false** depending upon whether the given number is a Narcissistic number in base 10.

Error checking for text strings or other invalid inputs is not required, only valid positive non-zero integers will be passed into the function. def narcissistic( value ):
	\nUse Call-Based format
[error] child: TypeError('sequence item 0: expected str instance, int found')
[code] def narcissistic(value):
    original_value = value
    sum_of_powers = 0
    power = len(str(value))

    while value > 0:
        digit = value % 10
        sum_of_powers += digit ** power
        value //= 10

    return sum_of_powers == original_value

# Test cases
print(narcissistic(153))  # True
print(narcissistic(1634))  # True
print(narcissistic(9474))  # True
print(narcissistic(9475))  # False

